printf - write formatted text

SYNOPSIS
    printf format [argument ...]

DESCRIPTION
    The format supports %s, %d, %c and %%. It recognizes \a, \b, \f,
    \n, \r, \t, \v and \\. Use one to three octal digits after a
    backslash or one to two hexadecimal digits after \x to write a
    byte. Escape sequences are interpreted in the format operand.

    The format repeats while there are unused arguments and the
    previous pass consumed an argument.

EXAMPLES
    printf '%s\n' alpha beta
    printf '\033[31mRED\033[0m\n'
    printf '\x1b[2J\x1b[H'

SEE ALSO
    sh(1)
